This is one of my favorite Steve Jobs videos of all time: Why the Japanese never talk about QUALITY. 

As an AI builder, some of the things we do (and spend tons of effort on) can't be talked about and shown visibly. 

For example: Our engineering team worked super hard to bring down the speed of responses to super-fast, sub-second levels -- now how do I talk about that or show it? 

Over the last few weeks, I have been working super hard to benchmark our RAG system against OpenAI using a new QUALITY metric OpenAI defined (it combines accuracy + hallucination to give a SAT-style score) -- this is painstaking work and does not show up in fancy marketing graphics .... but our customers notice it. 

If you are an engineer working on cool stuff, you *need* to have some of these *self belief* type metrics to motivate yourself (even if your boss - or the world - does not openly applaud you!) 

Keep building, my friends! 

